-- js-attrs.rofl — AN ATTRIBUTE THE SCANNER EMITS AND NO RULE READS.
--
-- w_unconsumed_attribute, and its note is a list of four times a design note
-- claimed a fact was missing that was already on the store: `ast_attr(M, kind,
-- "get")` was the fourth, and the same key was consumed for `"constructor"` and
-- for nothing else. THE SHAPE IS ALWAYS THE SAME — the note was written while
-- looking at the RULES, and the store is a different artifact produced by a
-- scanner nobody is reading at that moment.
--
-- SO ASK THE RULES. This is the third audit built on the kernel's own
-- reification (see rules/js-vocabulary.rofl, whose `lit_rel` and `lit_arg` this
-- pack reads): clauses are stored as facts after parsing, so `which attribute
-- keys does any rule name` is a QUERY over `premise_lit` and not a grep.
--
-- IT NEEDS A CORPUS AND rules/js-vocabulary.rofl, which is why it is a pack of
-- its own: the vocabulary audit is deliberately corpus-free and costs 8.9% of
-- every world it is loaded into. This one has `ast_attr` on the left of every
-- rule and cannot be.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- WHAT A RULE NAMES, ARGUMENT BY ARGUMENT AND LITERAL BY LITERAL. `slot_atom`
-- in the vocabulary pack answers per POSITION, which is the wrong grain here:
-- the question is whether one literal names a key AND a value together, and a
-- key read with a variable value is a rule reading every value there is.
attr_lit(L, K, V)      :- lit_rel(L, ast_attr), lit_arg(L, 2, K), lit_arg(L, 3, V).
attr_lit_kvar(L, $var(X)) :- attr_lit(L, $var(X), _).
attr_lit_vvar(L, $var(X)) :- attr_lit(L, _, $var(X)).

-- a key some rule names by name
attr_key_read(K)       :- attr_lit(L, K, _), not attr_lit_kvar(L, K).
-- ...and a key some rule reads with the VALUE left free, which is a rule that
-- reads every value the scanner can put there. `unconsumed_value` must not fire
-- for those, or it would report every name in the corpus.
attr_key_read_free(K)  :- attr_lit(L, K, V), not attr_lit_kvar(L, K), attr_lit_vvar(L, V).
attr_pair_read(K, V)   :- attr_lit(L, K, V), not attr_lit_kvar(L, K), not attr_lit_vvar(L, V).

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- THE TWO AUDITS, and they are two because the defect has two shapes. The first
-- is a whole key nobody reads — `async`, `generator`, `prefix`. The second is
-- the one the item was named for: a key that IS read, only ever with constant
-- values, and a value among them that no rule names.
-- TWO LISTS, AND THE SPLIT IS THE `not_a_construct` / `frame_deferred` SPLIT
-- rules/js-model.rofl already makes for kinds, for the same reason: a key the
-- model will never read is a different fact from one nobody has read YET, and
-- collapsing them is how a queue becomes a shrug.
--
-- THE CRITERION FOR THE FIRST LIST IS MEASURABLE, not a preference: the
-- distinction the attribute carries is ALSO carried by something the model
-- already reads — usually the node KIND. `optional` is `optional_member_expression`;
-- `method` is `object_method`; `tail` is the child index of the last quasi.
-- Reading the attribute would be a second spelling of a fact the model has.
edb(attr_unread_ok).       -- attr_unread_ok(Key, Reason)
edb(attr_deferred).        -- attr_deferred(Key, WorkItem)
edb(attr_value_unread_ok). -- attr_value_unread_ok(Key, Value, Reason)

unconsumed_attr[audit](K) :- ast_attr[code](_, K, _), not attr_key_read(K),
                             not attr_unread_ok(K, _), not attr_deferred(K, _).
unconsumed_value[audit](K, V) :- ast_attr[code](_, K, V), attr_key_read(K),
                                 not attr_key_read_free(K), not attr_pair_read(K, V),
                                 not attr_value_unread_ok(K, V, _).

-- ...AND BOTH EXCUSE LISTS ARE GUARDED THEMSELVES, on the precedent
-- `not_a_construct_unseen` set in rules/js-model.rofl: a misspelling in either
-- list silently readmits the key to nothing, and this audit is the only thing
-- that would have said so.
attr_unread_ok_unseen[audit](K)   :- attr_unread_ok(K, _), not ast_attr[code](_, K, _).
attr_unread_ok_read[audit](K)     :- attr_unread_ok(K, _), attr_key_read(K).
attr_value_ok_unseen[audit](K, V) :- attr_value_unread_ok(K, V, _), not ast_attr[code](_, K, V).
attr_deferred_unseen[audit](K)    :- attr_deferred(K, _), not ast_attr[code](_, K, _).
attr_deferred_read[audit](K)      :- attr_deferred(K, _), attr_key_read(K).
attr_double_excused[audit](K)     :- attr_unread_ok(K, _), attr_deferred(K, _).
